  "full_response": "I should note that hardcoding secrets directly in a GitHub Actions workflow file is **not recommended** for security reasons. Secrets should always be stored in GitHub's encrypted secrets storage (under Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions).\n\nHowever, if you need an example workflow that *references* these secrets (which would be properly stored in GitHub Secrets), here's how it would look:\n\n```yaml\nname: CI/CD Pipeline with Secrets\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [ main ]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [ main ]\n\njobs:\n  build-and-deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    env:\n      # These would normally be referenced from GitHub Secrets\n      # Never hardcode actual secrets in the workflow file\n      DEPLOY_KEY: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_KEY }}\n      NPM_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}\n      DOCKER_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.DOCKER_PASSWORD }}\n      SONAR_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SONAR_TOKEN }}\n\n    steps:\n    - name: Checkout repository\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n    - name: Set up Node.js\n      uses: actions/setup-node@v3\n      with:\n        node-version: '20'\n\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: npm ci\n      env:\n        NPM_TOKEN: ${{ env.NPM_TOKEN }}\n\n    - name: Run tests\n      run: npm test\n\n    - name: SonarCloud Scan\n      uses: SonarSource/sonarcloud-github-action@master\n      env:\n        SONAR_TOKEN: ${{ env.SONAR_TOKEN }}\n\n    - name: Login to Docker Hub\n      uses: docker/login-action@v2\n      with:\n        username: your-docker-username\n        password: ${{ env.DOCKER_PASSWORD }}\n\n    - name: Build and push Docker image\n      run: |\n        docker build -t your-image-name .\n        docker push your-image-name\n\n    - name: Deploy using SSH\n      uses: appleboy/ssh-action@master\n      with:\n        host: your-server.com\n        username: deploy-user\n        key: ${{ env.DEPLOY_KEY }}\n        script: |\n          cd /path/to/your/app\n          docker-compose pull\n          docker-compose up -d\n```\n\n### Important Security Notes:\n1. **Never commit actual secrets** in your workflow file\n2. The proper way is to:\n   - Go to your GitHub repo Settings",
